  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1259 AM CDT Thu Sep 17 2026\n\nAn upper level high will remain over the southeast/south central \nU.S. through the weekend. The upper level ridging over our \nregion will continue the near record to record heat through \nSunday, with highs in the middle 90s to around 100 degrees, and \nlows from around 70 to the middle 70s. These values are 14 to \nnear 20 degrees above normal, and the Heat Advisory will remain \nin effect through Sunday. \n\nA weak surface boundary sitting to our north may dip far enough\nsouth Friday to produce a few showers or storms in the\nafternoon, mainly in southwest Indiana and adjacent areas of\nsoutheast Illinois and northwest Kentucky. The model blend\nproduces 20-40% chances, with the best chances along and north\nof Interstate 64.\n\nOver the weekend, the upper ridge will slowly start breaking down as \nan upper low over the northwestern U.S. slowly pushes eastward. The \nlow will move over the Great Lakes region by 12z Tuesday with a weak \ntrof extending southward, while a weak surface low/cold front pushes \nthrough the middle Mississippi and lower Ohio valleys Monday into \nTuesday. The model blend spreads 30-40% chances of showers and \nthunderstorms across the PAH forecast area Monday afternoon through \nMonday evening, with 20-30% chances continuing late Monday night \nthrough Tuesday evening. Isolated chances will persist into \nWednesday.",
